     <date year="1971" month="May" day="27"/>
     <abstract pn="section-abstract">
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-1">IEEE Computer Society Workshop<br/>
+West Coast Committee</t>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-2">COMPUTER NETWORKS</t>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-3">Lake Arrowhead, California<br/>
+September 8 - September 10, 1971</t>
+      <dl newline="false" spacing="normal" indent="3" pn="section-abstract-4">
+        <dt pn="section-abstract-4.1">Co-Chairmen:</dt>
+        <dd pn="section-abstract-4.2">David J. Farber -- University of California, Irvine<br/>
+Stephen D. Crocker -- ARPA/IPT</dd>
+      </dl>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-5">The number of networks has grown to the point where not all
+participants are familiar with each other; more networks are under
+development. This workshop is intended especially for those
+manufactureers, users and researchers who have just entered, or are
+about to enter, the network field.  Presentations are invited on all
+aspects of computer networks, particularly including user
+communities, inter-node protocols, terminal and switching equipments,
+and communications technology.</t>
+      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-6">Presentations on embryonic systems are especially invited.</t>
     </abstract>
